{%- comment -%}
  card-product.liquid — the product card.

  Renders nothing when `product` is blank. A freshly installed theme has no
  products, and a card that invents a name and a price for a shoe that does
  not exist would put fabricated commercial data in front of a shopper —
  callers are responsible for their own empty state (see empty-state.liquid).

  One tab stop per card: the title carries a stretched ::after that covers
  the card, and the image link is removed from the tab order. Quick add adds
  a second stop only where it is a genuinely new action — see the comment on
  the action block below.

  Params:
    product      (product, optional) — nothing renders when blank
    sizes        (string, optional)
    loading      (string, optional)
    show_badges  (boolean, optional) — default true
    heading_tag  (string, optional)  — h2/h3/h4, default h3

  `heading_tag` exists so the card does not create a gap in the document
  outline. On the homepage a card sits under a section <h2>, so <h3> is right.
  On a collection page the only heading above it is the page <h1>, so the
  caller passes h2 — otherwise the outline jumps h1 to h3 and a screen-reader
  user hears a level that was never opened.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign show_card_badges = show_badges | default: true, allow_false: true
  assign title_tag = heading_tag | default: 'h3'

  assign ratio_class = 'media--portrait'
  case settings.card_image_ratio
    when 'square'
      assign ratio_class = 'media--square'
    when 'landscape'
      assign ratio_class = 'media--landscape'
  endcase

  assign zoom_class = ''
  if settings.enable_image_zoom
    assign zoom_class = ' media--zoom'
  endif

  comment
    image-fallback's shared default srcset (360,540,720,…) is tuned for
    full-bleed media — a card thumbnail never renders anywhere near that
    wide, and the 360-to-540 jump overshoots a mobile grid cell by 2-3x once
    device pixel ratio is applied. This list adds the finer low-end steps a
    card actually needs and caps out well short of a hero image's ceiling.

    Low end tightened further after grid-sizes.liquid started reporting a
    real width: a 2-column mobile grid cell lands around 170px, and even
    with an accurate `sizes` hint, a bare 280/360 jump still overshoots it
    by a full step once DPR is applied. 160/240/320 close that gap without
    stretching the ladder past what a card ever legitimately needs.
  endcomment
  assign card_widths = '160,200,240,280,320,360,450,540,650,780,940,1130,1360'
-%}

{%- if product != blank and product.id -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign second_image = product.media[1]
    assign show_hover = false
    if settings.card_hover_image and second_image != blank and second_image.media_type == 'image'
      assign show_hover = true
    endif

    assign material = product.metafields.custom.material.value
    assign is_new = false
    if product.tags contains 'new'
      assign is_new = true
    endif
  -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The GA4 item for select_item and view_item_list (§9.8). Renders as an
    empty string when the data layer is off, so a store that is not measuring
    does not pay for the attribute on every card in every grid.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture analytics_item -%}
    {%- render 'analytics-events', scope: 'item', product: product -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Compare payload. Captured once here rather than rebuilt in JavaScript —
    Liquid already knows the merchant's own money format, and re-implementing
    it client-side is exactly the mistake variant-picker's own comment warns
    against for price.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture compare_payload -%}
    {
      "handle": {{ product.handle | json }},
      "title": {{ product.title | json }},
      "url": {{ product.url | json }},
      "image": {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 200 | json }},
      "price": {{ product.price | money | json }},
      "material": {{ material | json }},
      "footprint": {{ product.metafields.custom.carbon_footprint | json }},
      "available": {{ product.available | json }}
    }
  {%- endcapture -%}

  <div
    class="card card-product"
    {% if analytics_item != blank %}data-analytics-item="{{ analytics_item | strip | escape }}"{% endif %}
  >
    <a
      class="card-product__media media {{ ratio_class }}{{ zoom_class }}"
      href="{{ product.url }}"
      tabindex="-1"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      {%- render 'image-fallback',
        image: product.featured_media,
        alt: product.title,
        sizes: sizes,
        widths: card_widths,
        loading: loading
      -%}

      {%- if show_hover -%}
        <span class="card-product__hover">
          {%- render 'image-fallback',
            image: second_image,
            alt: product.title,
            sizes: sizes,
            widths: card_widths
          -%}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>

    {%- comment -%}
      Quick view. A genuinely different action from quick add (preview vs.
      commit), so — like quick add — it earns its own tab stop rather than
      folding into the card's one stretched link. Sits over the media, so it
      needs its own z-index above the title's stretched ::after (see
      `.card__action` above) and a background of its own: an icon alone has
      no guaranteed contrast against arbitrary product photography.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.card_quick_view -%}
      <quick-view-trigger
        data-url="{{ product.url }}"
        data-error-message="{{ 'products.product.quick_view_error' | t | escape }}"
      >
        <button
          type="button"
          class="card-product__quick-view icon-button"
          aria-label="{{ 'products.product.quick_view_label' | t: title: product.title | escape }}"
        >
          {%- render 'icon', icon: 'eye' -%}
        </button>
      </quick-view-trigger>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Compare. A genuinely different action from quick view or quick add —
      it does not open anything or add anything, only marks the product for
      later — so it earns its own tab stop the same way those two already do.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.card_show_compare -%}
      <compare-toggle
        data-compare="{{ compare_payload | strip | escape }}"
        data-added-message="{{ 'products.product.compare_added' | t | escape }}"
        data-removed-message="{{ 'products.product.compare_removed' | t | escape }}"
        data-full-message="{{ 'products.product.compare_full' | t | escape }}"
      >
        <button
          type="button"
          class="card-product__compare icon-button"
          aria-pressed="false"
          aria-label="{{ 'products.product.compare_add_label' | t: title: product.title | escape }}"
        >
          {%- render 'icon', icon: 'compare' -%}
        </button>
      </compare-toggle>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_card_badges -%}
      <div class="badge-row">
        {%- if product.available == false and settings.card_show_sold_out_badge -%}
          <span class="badge badge--sold-out">{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}</span>
        {%- elsif product.compare_at_price > product.price and settings.card_show_sale_badge -%}
          <span class="badge badge--sale">{{ 'products.product.on_sale' | t }}</span>
        {%- elsif is_new and settings.card_show_new_badge -%}
          <span class="badge">{{ 'products.product.new' | t }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="card__body">
      <{{ title_tag }} class="card-product__title h5">
        <a class="card__link" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a>
      </{{ title_tag }}>

      {%- if settings.card_show_material and material != blank -%}
        {%- render 'material-tag',
          material: material,
          composition: product.metafields.custom.material_composition.value,
          story: product.metafields.custom.material_story.value,
          compact: true
        -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if settings.card_show_swatches -%}
        {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
          {%- assign option_name = option.name | downcase -%}
          {%- if option_name contains 'color' or option_name contains 'colour' -%}
            <ul class="swatches" aria-label="{{ option.name | escape }}">
              {%- for value in option.values limit: 5 -%}
                <li
                  class="swatches__dot"
                  {% if value.swatch.image %}
                    style="background-image: url({{ value.swatch.image | image_url: width: 24 }});"
                  {% elsif value.swatch.color %}
                    style="--swatch: {{ value.swatch.color }};"
                  {% endif %}
                  title="{{ value | escape }}"
                >
                  <span class="visually-hidden">{{ value }}</span>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- render 'price', product: product, show_from: true -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Quick add (§9.2 rule 6). Three states, and the disabled one says why
        rather than sitting there dead:

          sold out       → disabled button labelled Sold out
          one variant    → real POST form, adds without leaving the page
          many variants  → Choose options, routed to the PDP

        The multi-variant link is `tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"`: it goes
        to the same URL as the card title, so exposing it again would put two
        identical stops in the tab order for no gain. Touch users still get
        the affordance without hovering, which is what §9.4 asks for, and
        keyboard and screen-reader users keep the one stop per card promised
        in §8. The single-variant button is a genuinely different action, so
        it earns its own stop.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if settings.card_quick_add -%}
        <div class="card__action">
          {%- if product.available == false -%}
            <button class="button button--secondary button--full" type="button" disabled>
              {{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}
            </button>
          {%- elsif product.variants.size == 1 -%}
            {%- assign quick_add_label = 'products.product.quick_add_label' | t: title: product.title -%}
            <product-form data-success-message="{{ 'products.product.added_to_cart' | t | escape }}">
              {%- form 'product', product, class: 'card__action-form', novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
                <input
                  type="hidden"
                  name="id"
                  value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
                >
                <button
                  class="button button--secondary button--full"
                  type="submit"
                  name="add"
                  aria-label="{{ quick_add_label | escape }}"
                >
                  {{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}
                </button>
              {%- endform -%}
            </product-form>
          {%- else -%}
            <a
              class="button button--secondary button--full"
              href="{{ product.url }}"
              tabindex="-1"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              {{ 'products.product.choose_options' | t }}
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

{%- endif -%}
